evidence.text:
If your site serves the same page at `/pricing` and `/pricing/`, or at `/` and `/index.html`, the **Top Pages** report lists them as separate pages. The best fix is a 301 redirect so each page has a single address. If you can't change how your site handles its URLs, you can merge them in your snippet instead:

```javascript
function transformRequest(payload) {
  var url = new URL(payload.u)
  // Count /index.html as the folder it's in
  url.pathname = url.pathname.replace(/\/index\.html?$/, '/')
  // Remove the trailing slash from every path except the homepage
  if (url.pathname.length > 1) {
    url.pathname = url.pathname.replace(/\/+$/, '')
  }
  payload.u = url.toString()
  return payload
}

// At the end, update plausible.init call
plausible.init({
  transformRequest: transformRequest
})
```

This works on the address already in each event, so you don't need to disable automatic pageviews and it also works in single-page applications. Query parameters such as UTM tags are kept.

A few things to keep in mind:

* It applies to every event, so your goals, filters and funnels see the merged paths too. Update any pageview goal that ends with a slash, such as `/thank-you/`, to the path without it.
* It only changes pageviews sent after you add it. To combine older stats, filter by **Page** and select both versions of the path.
